      "writtenOn": "2023-04-08T04:10:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the confusing logic here.\n\nThe idea here is to keep track of all the netlink message and use it to create the link property. The call stack is `processRtNetlinkAddressMessage` -\u003e `updateInterfaceAddress` -\u003e `maybeUpdateTetheringSocketAddress`. \n\nIn `maybeUpdateTetheringSocketAddress`, we check wehther the link property change is for certain tethering interface or not. So the normal upperstream network won\u0027t trigger any `updateSocketInfoAddress`.\n\nWe cannot determine wether the NetLinkMessage is for normal upper stream network or tehtering downstream network when we receive the message. Because at that time, we might not receive the callback from NetworkCallback or TetheringEventCallback yet, so we need to cache every netlink update for future usage.",
      "parentUuid": "69e87e28_0f98c68a",
      "revId": "6ee4442e9891201186514a0912b325656c7d12bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
