      },
      "lineNbr": 346,
      "author": {
        "id": 1758351
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-08T04:10:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we have discussed the similar point in the previous comment. \n\nIt won\u0027t simplify the logic because when creating the NetworkKey, because you will need to have the conversion between interfaceIdx and interfaceName in one place anyway. We also need to maintain the mLocalOnlyInterfaces and mTetheredInterfaces separately. Changing this place will result in managing mLocalOnlyInterfaces and mTetheredInterfaces separately.\n\nI have tired the merging the mTetherInterfaceSockets and mNetworkSockets before but it make the code even more complicated. So I revert it back.\n\nAlso, put the index into the NetworkKey is like a `cache` the index -\u003e ifaceName mapping. It will facing similar race condition you mentioned in other comment.\n\nI gave up cache on anything. Maybe we can talk offline to have better consensus on it.",
      "parentUuid": "de660449_cf217657",
