        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-05T07:02:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ifaces are added from the netlink callbacks, which are not synchronized with the tethering callbacks, so there could be races where an interface was toggled, and the 2nd ID gets removed here even though this is the callback for the first interface that has the 1st ID.\n\nI think adding/removing interfaces in updateInterfaceAddress would avoid that.",
      "revId": "6ee4442e9891201186514a0912b325656c7d12bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b637ca27_e2a27cf7",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/connectivity/mdns/MdnsSocketProvider.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 404,
      "author": {
        "id": 1758351
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-08T04:10:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doing the coversion in `updateInterfaceAddress` will have similar issue.\n\nThe `updateInterfaceAddress` using index and will need the ifaceName to know if it is a tethering interface or not. The ifaceName will get updated in the tethering interface callback. So the unsync situation will just happened reversely.\n\nIt seems like the cache related race condition is really non-trivial. I believe the logic I have here is right but it is too hard to explain it to others(maybe I also miss other cases). \n\nTo make the logic more confident, I removed the cache. Always get the latest up to date ifaceIndexName. I hope it will make the logic less complicated.",
      "parentUuid": "712b3320_e313e44f",
      "revId": "6ee4442e9891201186514a0912b325656c7d12bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
